{"case_id":"C033","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration-boundary","input-semantics"],"confidence":91,"affected_functions":["fuzz_swizzle_ycck","wuffs_base__pixel_config__set","wuffs_base__pixel_config__pixbuf_len"],"reason":"S1 explicitly defines 0xFFFFFF as the maximum supported image width or height and documents arithmetic-safety properties at that boundary, but H0 exercises pixel configurations only with x_max_excl and y_max_excl at most 64. It therefore misses the dimension-limit protocol, including values at 0xFFFFFF and immediately outside the supported range, plus the associated size calculations.","evidence":["S1 defines WUFFS_BASE__IMAGE__DIMENSION_MAX_INCL as 0xFFFFFF and identifies it as the largest supported width or height.","S1 specifically documents 32 * N and 32 * N * N overflow properties, making boundary-sensitive memory-requirement calculations relevant.","fuzz_swizzle_ycck derives x_min_incl, x_max_excl, y_min_incl, and y_max_excl from 6-bit hash fields and constrains the resulting maxima to at most 64 before calling wuffs_base__pixel_config__set.","H0 calls wuffs_base__pixel_config__pixbuf_len only for those small configurations and never supplies dimensions near, equal to, or greater than WUFFS_BASE__IMAGE__DIMENSION_MAX_INCL."],"recommended_action":"Add a boundary-focused harness path for wuffs_base__pixel_config__set and wuffs_base__pixel_config__pixbuf_len using dimensions around 0xFFFFFF, including 0, 0xFFFFFE, 0xFFFFFF, and 0x1000000, without requiring allocation of the reported pixel buffer."}
